qcom-hv-haptics: haptics_get_status_data(): name uninitialised for unknown selectors

For a selector outside 0..BRAKE_CAL_SCALAR and the three named ones, 'name' was used
uninitialised by dev_dbg() and trace_qcom_haptics_status() (the tracepoint copies the
string: a wild pointer dereference). Use "UNKNOWN_STS". (clang: -Wsometimes-uninitialized)

--- a/bsp612/soc-repo/drivers/input/misc/qcom-hv-haptics.c
+++ b/bsp612/soc-repo/drivers/input/misc/qcom-hv-haptics.c
@@ -1271,6 +1271,8 @@
 		name = "FIFO_REAL_TIME_STS";
 	else if (sel == AUTO_BRAKE_CAL_STS)
 		name = "AUTO_BRAKE_CAL_STS";
+	else
+		name = "UNKNOWN_STS";
 
 	dev_dbg(chip->dev, "Get status data[%s] = (%#x, %#x)\n", name, data[0], data[1]);
 	trace_qcom_haptics_status(name, data[0], data[1]);
